DG.put("bachitr-naatak/1",{"n":1,"title":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਾਲ ਜੀ ਕੀ ਉਸਤਤਿ।","title_roman":"Sree kaal jee kee usatti |","page":135,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"announcement","name":"ਅਥ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਲਿਖ੍ਯਤੇ","gurmukhi":"ਅਥ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਲਿਖ੍ਯਤੇ।","roman":"Ath bachitr naatak granth likhyate |","meaning_en":"Here begins the book Bachittar Natak (the Wondrous Drama).","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"invocation","gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਮੁਖਵਾਕ ਪਾਤਸਾਹੀ ੧੦","roman":"Sree mukhvaak paatsaahee 10","meaning_en":"Uttered by the sacred mouth of the Tenth Master.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ । ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Tvaprasaadi | dohraa","meaning_en":"By Your grace. Dohra.","page":135,"invocation":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ","meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1],"number_text":"੧।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਖੜਗ ਕੋ ਕਰੌ ਸੁ ਹਿਤੁ ਚਿਤੁ ਲਾਇ।","roman":"Namaskaar sree kharag ko karau su hitu chitu laai |","meaning_en":"I bow to the revered Sword, with love and with my whole mind:","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਖੜਗ: the Sword, here a name of God as the power that destroys evil."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਰਨ ਕਰੌ ਗਿਰੰਥ ਇਹੁ ਤੁਮ ਮੁਹਿ ਕਰਹੁ ਸਹਾਇ। ੧।","roman":"Pooran karau giranth ihu tum muhi karhu sahaai | 1 |","meaning_en":"may I complete this book; You be my help.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"section_heading","name":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਾਲ ਜੀ ਕੀ ਉਸਤਤਿ।","gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਾਲ ਜੀ ਕੀ ਉਸਤਤਿ।","roman":"Sree kaal jee kee usatti |","meaning_en":"In praise of the revered Kaal (the Timeless Lord).","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤ੍ਰਿਭੰਗੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿਭੰਗੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tribhangee chhand","meaning_en":"Tribhangi metre.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2],"number_text":"੨।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਗ ਖੰਡ ਬਿਹੰਡੰ ਖਲਦਲ ਖੰਡੰ ਅਤਿ ਰਣ ਮੰਡੰ ਬਰਬੰਡੰ।","roman":"Khag khand bihandan khaldal khandan ati ran mandan barbandan |","meaning_en":"The sword cuts and destroys, it crushes the hosts of the wicked, it adorns the battlefield, mighty and powerful;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਹੰਡੰ: smashes; ਬਰਬੰਡੰ: very strong. The sword is addressed as a form of the divine power."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜ ਦੰਗ ਅਖੰਡੰ ਤੇਜ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡੰ ਜੋਤਿ ਅਮੰਡੰ ਭਾਨੁ ਪ੍ਰਭੰ।","roman":"Bhuj dang akhandan tej prachandan joti amandan bhaanu prabhan |","meaning_en":"unbreakable is its arm-staff, fierce its brilliance, its light unrivalled, radiant like the sun;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭੁਜ ਦੰਗ: read as 'staff in the arm' or 'mighty in arm'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਖ ਸੰਤਾ ਕਰਣੰ ਦੁਰਮਤਿ ਦਰਣੰ ਕਿਲਬਿਖ ਹਰਣੰ ਅਸਿ ਸਰਣੰ।","roman":"Sukh santaa karnan duramti darnan kilbikh harnan asi sarnan |","meaning_en":"it brings peace to saints, it crushes evil-mindedness, it removes sins: I seek the refuge of the Sword.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਸਿ ਸਰਣੰ: 'the sword is my refuge'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈ ਜੈ ਜਗ ਕਾਰਣ ਸ੍ਰਿਸਟਿ ਉਬਾਰਣ ਮਮ ਪ੍ਰਤਿਪਾਰਣ ਜੈ ਤੇਗੰ। ੨।","roman":"Jai jai jag kaaran sristi ubaaran mam pratipaaran jai tegan | 2 |","meaning_en":"Hail, hail, Cause of the world, Saviour of creation, my Sustainer: hail to the Sword!","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[3],"number_text":"੩।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਦਾ ਏਕ ਜੋਤ੍ਯੰ ਅਜੂਨੀ ਸਰੂਪੰ। ਮਹਾਦੇਵ ਦੇਵੰ ਮਹਾ ਭੂਪ ਭੂਪੰ।","roman":"Sadaa ek jotyan ajoonee saroopan | mahaadev devan mahaa bhoop bhoopan |","meaning_en":"Ever one Light, of unborn form, God of the great gods, King of the great kings;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹਾਦੇਵ ਦੇਵੰ: the God even of Mahadev (Shiva) and the gods."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ ਨਿਰੂਪੰ ਨ੍ਰਿਬਾਣੰ। ਕਲੰ ਕਾਰਣੇਯੰ ਨਮੋ ਖੜਗਪਾਣੰ। ੩।","roman":"Nirankaar nityan niroopan nribaanan | kalan kaarneyan namo kharagpaanan | 3 |","meaning_en":"formless, eternal, beyond description, free (beyond release); the cause of all power: salutation to the One with the sword in hand.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨ੍ਰਿਬਾਣੰ: read as 'in nirvana / free', or 'without arrows (needing no weapon)'. ਕਲੰ ਕਾਰਣੇਯੰ: cause of power (ਕਲਾ), or cause of all. ਖੜਗਪਾਣੰ: whose hand holds the sword."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[4],"number_text":"੪।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਨ੍ਰਿਬਿਕਾਰ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ ਨਿਰਾਲੰ। ਨ ਬ੍ਰਿਧੰ ਬਿਸੇਖੰ ਨ ਤਰੁਨੰ ਨ ਬਾਲੰ।","roman":"Nirankaar nribikaar nityan niraalan | na bridhan bisekhan na tarunan na baalan |","meaning_en":"Formless, without defect, eternal, distinct from all; not particularly old, not young, not a child;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਰੰਕੰ ਨ ਰਾਯੰ ਨ ਰੂਪੰ ਨ ਰੇਖੰ। ਨ ਰੰਗੰ ਨ ਰਾਗੰ ਅਪਾਰੰ ਅਭੇਖੰ। ੪।","roman":"Na rankan na raayan na roopan na rekhan | na rangan na raagan apaaran abhekhan | 4 |","meaning_en":"not a pauper, not a king, without form or outline, without colour or attachment, boundless, without garb.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[5],"number_text":"੫।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਰੂਪੰ ਨ ਰੇਖੰ ਨ ਰੰਗੰ ਨ ਰਾਗੰ। ਨ ਨਾਮੰ ਨ ਠਾਮੰ ਮਹਾ ਜੋਤਿ ਜਾਗੰ।","roman":"Na roopan na rekhan na rangan na raagan | na naaman na thaaman mahaa joti jaagan |","meaning_en":"No form, no outline, no colour, no attachment; no name, no place: a great Light, ever awake;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਦ੍ਵੈਖੰ ਨ ਭੇਖੰ ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ। ਮਹਾ ਜੋਗ ਜੋਗੰ ਸੁ ਪਰਮੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਯੰ। ੫।","roman":"Na dvaikhan na bhekhan nirankaar nityan | mahaa jog jogan su parman pavityan | 5 |","meaning_en":"no hatred, no garb, formless and eternal; the Yogi of the great yogis, supremely pure.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਵੈਖੰ: enmity, hatred (ਦ੍ਵੇਸ਼)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[6],"number_text":"੬।","page":135,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਜੇਯੰ ਅਭੇਯੰ ਅਨਾਮੰ ਅਠਾਮੰ। ਮਹਾਜੋਗ ਜੋਗੰ ਮਹਾ ਕਾਮ ਕਾਮੰ।","roman":"Ajeyan abheyan anaaman athaaman | mahaajog jogan mahaa kaam kaaman |","meaning_en":"Unconquerable, beyond division, nameless, placeless; the Yogi of great yogis, the Desire of all desires;","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹਾ ਕਾਮ ਕਾਮੰ: read as 'the fulfiller of desires' or 'more beautiful than Kamdev'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਲੇਖੰ ਅਭੇਖੰ ਅਨੀਲੰ ਅਨਾਦੰ। ਪਰੇਯੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ ਸਦਾ ਨ੍ਰਿਬਿਖਾਦੰ। ੬।","roman":"Alekhan abhekhan aneelan anaadan | pareyan pavitran sadaa nribikhaadan | 6 |","meaning_en":"beyond account, without garb, colourless, without beginning; beyond all, pure, ever free of sorrow.","page":135,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[7],"number_text":"੭।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਆਦੰ ਅਨਾਦੰ ਅਨੀਲੰ ਅਨੰਤੰ। ਅਦ੍ਵੈਖੰ ਅਭੇਖੰ ਮਹੇਸੰ ਮਹੰਤੰ।","roman":"Suaadan anaadan aneelan anantan | advaikhan abhekhan mahesan mahantan |","meaning_en":"Of excellent beginning, yet without beginning, colourless, infinite; without hatred, without garb, the great Lord, the Great One;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਆਦੰ: read as 'the excellent primal one' or 'the taste (delight) of all'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਰੋਖੰ ਨ ਸੋਖੰ ਨ ਦ੍ਰੋਹੰ ਨ ਮੋਹੰ। ਨ ਕਾਮੰ ਨ ਕ੍ਰੋਧੰ ਅਜੋਨੀ ਅਜੋਹੰ। ੭।","roman":"Na rokhan na sokhan na drohan na mohan | na kaaman na krodhan ajonee ajohan | 7 |","meaning_en":"no anger, no sorrow, no malice, no attachment; no lust, no wrath; not born, and needing to look at nothing.","page":136,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"},{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੋਖੰ: read as 'sorrow (ਸੋਗ)' or 'drying up'. ਅਜੋਹੰ: read as 'beyond seeing' or 'who has no one to look to'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[8],"number_text":"੮।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰੇਯੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ ਪੁਨੀਤੰ ਪੁਰਾਣੰ। ਅਜੇਯੰ ਅਭੇਯੰ ਭਵਿਖ੍ਯੰ ਭਵਾਣੰ।","roman":"Pareyan pavitran puneetan puraanan | ajeyan abheyan bhavikhyan bhavaanan |","meaning_en":"Beyond all, pure, holy, ancient; unconquerable, undivided, in the future and the present;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਰੋਗੰ ਨ ਸੋਗੰ ਸੁ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ ਨਵੀਨੰ। ਅਜਾਯੰ ਸਹਾਯੰ ਪਰਮੰ ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨੰ। ੮।","roman":"Na rogan na sogan su nityan naveenan | ajaayan sahaayan parman prabeenan | 8 |","meaning_en":"no disease, no sorrow, ever new; unborn, the helper of all, supremely wise.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[9],"number_text":"੯।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਭੂਤੰ ਭਵਿਖ੍ਯੰ ਭਵਾਨੰ ਭਵੇਯੰ। ਨਮੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਬਕਾਰੰ ਨਮੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਜੁਰੇਯੰ।","roman":"Su bhootan bhavikhyan bhavaanan bhaveyan | namo nribkaaran namo nrijureyan |","meaning_en":"He is in the past, the future and the present. Salutation to the One without defect, salutation to the One free of fever (affliction).","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨ੍ਰਿਜੁਰੇਯੰ: free of fever / old age (ਜੁਰ)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵੰ ਨਮੋ ਰਾਜ ਰਾਜੰ। ਨਿਰਾਲੰਬ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ ਸੁ ਰਾਜਾਧਿਰਾਜੰ।੯।","roman":"Namo dev devan namo raaj raajan | niraalanb nityan su raajaadhiraajan | 9 |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the God of gods, salutation to the King of kings; needing no support, eternal, the supreme Sovereign.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[10],"number_text":"੧੦।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਲੇਖੰ ਅਭੇਖੰ ਅਭੂਤੰ ਅਦ੍ਵੈਖੰ। ਨ ਰਾਗੰ ਨ ਰੰਗੰ ਨ ਰੂਪੰ ਨ ਰੇਖੰ।","roman":"Alekhan abhekhan abhootan advaikhan | na raagan na rangan na roopan na rekhan |","meaning_en":"Beyond account, without garb, not of the elements, without hatred; no attachment, no colour, no form, no outline;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵ ਮਹਾ ਜੋਗ ਜੋਗੰ। ਮਹਾ ਕਾਮ ਕਾਮੰ ਮਹਾ ਭੋਗ ਭੋਗੰ। ੧੦।","roman":"Mahaa dev dev mahaa jog jogan | mahaa kaam kaaman mahaa bhog bhogan | 10 |","meaning_en":"the God of the great gods, the Yogi of the great yogis, the Desire of great desires, the Enjoyer of great enjoyments.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The edition prints ਦੇਵ (without tippi) in 'ਮਹਾ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵ', kept as printed."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[11],"number_text":"੧੧।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਰਾਜਸੰ ਤਾਮਸੰ ਸਾਤਕੇਯੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨਾਰਿ ਕੋ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰੇ ਨਰੇਯੰ।","roman":"Kahoon raajsan taamsan saatkeyan | kahoon naari ko roop dhaare nareyan |","meaning_en":"Somewhere He is of the quality of activity, of darkness, of goodness; somewhere He has taken the form of a woman, or of a man;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਾਜਸ, ਤਾਮਸ, ਸਾਤਕ: the three qualities (rajas, tamas, sattva)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਦੇਵੀਯੰ ਦੇਵਤੰ ਦਈਤ ਰੂਪੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਰੂਪੰ ਅਨੇਕ ਧਾਰੇ ਅਨੂਪੰ। ੧੧।","roman":"Kahoon deveeyan devtan daeet roopan | kahoon roopan anek dhaare anoopan | 11 |","meaning_en":"somewhere the form of a goddess, a god, a demon; somewhere He has taken many incomparable forms.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[12],"number_text":"੧੨।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਫੂਲ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਭਲੇ ਰਾਜ ਫੂਲੇ। ਕਹੂੰ ਭਵਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਭਲੀ ਭਾਤਿ ਭੂਲੇ।","roman":"Kahoon phool hvai kai bhale raaj phoole | kahoon bhavar hvai kai bhalee bhaati bhoole |","meaning_en":"Somewhere, becoming a flower, He blooms in fine splendour; somewhere, becoming a bumble-bee, He is wholly enchanted (by it);","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭੂਲੇ: lost in, infatuated (the bee lost in the flower)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਪਵਨ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਬਹੇ ਬੇਗਿ ਐਸੇ। ਕਹੇ ਮੋ ਨ ਆਵੇ ਕਥੌ ਤਾਹਿ ਕੈਸੇ। ੧੨।","roman":"Kahoon pavan hvai kai bahe begi aise | kahe mo na aave kathau taahi kaise | 12 |","meaning_en":"somewhere, becoming the wind, He blows so swiftly; He cannot be described, so how can I tell of Him?","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[13],"number_text":"੧੩।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨਾਦ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਭਲੀ ਭਾਂਤਿ ਬਾਜੇ। ਕਹੂੰ ਪਾਰਧੀ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਧਰੇ ਬਾਨ ਰਾਜੇ।","roman":"Kahoon naad hvai kai bhalee bhaanti baaje | kahoon paardhee hvai dhare baan raaje |","meaning_en":"Somewhere, becoming sound, He plays beautifully; somewhere, becoming a hunter, He holds the arrow in splendour;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਭਲੀ ਭਾਤਿ ਮੋਹੇ। ਕਹੂੰ ਕਾਮਕੀ ਜਿਉ ਧਰੇ ਰੂਪ ਸੋਹੇ। ੧੩।","roman":"Kahoon mrig hvai kai bhalee bhaati mohe | kahoon kaamkee jiu dhare roop sohe | 13 |","meaning_en":"somewhere, becoming a deer, He is wholly enchanted (by the sound); somewhere He appears beautiful like Kamdev (Cupid).","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਮਕੀ: read as 'like Kamdev, the god of love'; some read 'like a lover'. The image: the deer is lured by the hunter's sound, and He is both."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[14],"number_text":"੧੪।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਜਾਨਿ ਜਾਈ ਕਛੂ ਰੂਪ ਰੇਖੰ। ਕਹਾ ਬਾਸ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਫਿਰੈ ਕਉਨ ਭੇਖੰ।","roman":"Nahee jaani jaaee kachhoo roop rekhan | kahaa baas taa ko phirai kaun bhekhan |","meaning_en":"Nothing of His form or outline can be known; where does He dwell, in what garb does He wander?","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਾ ਨਾਮ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਕਹਾ ਕੈ ਕਹਾਵੈ। ਕਹਾ ਮੈ ਬਖਾਨੋ ਕਹੇ ਮੋ ਨ ਆਵੈ। ੧੪।","roman":"Kahaa naam taa ko kahaa kai kahaavai | kahaa mai bakhaano kahe mo na aavai | 14 |","meaning_en":"What is His name, by what is He called? What can I say? He cannot be described.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[15],"number_text":"੧੫।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਤਾਕੋ ਕੋਈ ਤਾਤ ਮਾਤੰ ਨ ਭਾਯੰ। ਨ ਪੁਤ੍ਰੰ ਨ ਪੌਤ੍ਰੰ ਨ ਦਾਯਾ ਨ ਦਾਯੰ।","roman":"Na taako koee taat maatan na bhaayan | na putran na pautran na daayaa na daayan |","meaning_en":"He has no father, mother or brother; no son, no grandson, no nurse, no nursemaid;","page":136,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਾਯਾ ਨ ਦਾਯੰ: read as 'no nurse and no nursemaid' or 'no kin and no heir'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਨੇਹੰ ਨ ਗੇਹੰ ਨ ਸੈਨੰ ਨ ਸਾਥੰ। ਮਹਾ ਰਾਜ ਰਾਜੰ ਮਹਾ ਨਾਥ ਨਾਥੰ। ੧੫।","roman":"Na nehan na gehan na sainan na saathan | mahaa raaj raajan mahaa naath naathan | 15 |","meaning_en":"no attachment, no home, no army, no companion; He is the great King of kings, the great Master of masters.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[16],"number_text":"੧੬।","page":136,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਮੰ ਪੁਰਾਨੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ ਪਰੇਯੰ। ਅਨਾਦੰ ਅਨੀਲੰ ਅਸੰਭੰ ਅਜੇਯੰ।","roman":"Parman puraanan pavitran pareyan | anaadan aneelan asanbhan ajeyan |","meaning_en":"Supreme, ancient, pure, beyond all; without beginning, colourless, unborn, unconquerable;","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਭੇਦੰ ਅਛੇਦੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਥੰ। ਮਹਾ ਦੀਨ ਦੀਨੰ ਮਹਾ ਨਾਥ ਨਾਥੰ। ੧੬।","roman":"Abhedan achhedan pavitran pramaathan | mahaa deen deenan mahaa naath naathan | 16 |","meaning_en":"undivided, indestructible, pure, the Crusher (of evil); the great support of the humble, the great Master of masters.","page":136,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹਾ ਦੀਨ ਦੀਨੰ: read as 'protector of the most humble' or 'the faith of faiths (ਦੀਨ)'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[17],"number_text":"੧੭।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਦਾਗੰ ਅਦਗੰ ਅਲੇਖੰ ਅਭੇਖੰ। ਅਨੰਤੰ ਅਨੀਲੰ ਅਰੂਪੰ ਅਦ੍ਵੈਖੰ।","roman":"Adaagan adgan alekhan abhekhan | anantan aneelan aroopan advaikhan |","meaning_en":"Without blemish, beyond burning, beyond account, without garb; infinite, colourless, formless, without hatred;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਦਾਗੰ: without stain; ਅਦਗੰ: read as 'who cannot be burnt' or 'who cannot be deceived'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਤੇਜ ਤੇਜੰ ਮਹਾ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਜ੍ਵਾਲੰ। ਮਹਾ ਤੰਤ੍ਰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਮਹਾ ਕਾਲ ਕਾਲੰ। ੧੭।","roman":"Mahaa tej tejan mahaa jvaal jvaalan | mahaa tantr mantr mahaa kaal kaalan | 17 |","meaning_en":"the Light of great lights, the Flame of great flames, the great Tantra and Mantra, the great Death of death.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[18],"number_text":"੧੮।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੰ ਬਾਮ ਚਾਪਿਯੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣੰ ਕਰਾਲੰ। ਮਹਾ ਤੇਜ ਤੇਜੰ ਬਿਰਾਜੈ ਬਿਸਾਲੰ।","roman":"Karan baam chaapiyan kripaanan karaalan | mahaa tej tejan biraajai bisaalan |","meaning_en":"In His left hand the bow, the fearsome sword; the Light of great lights, He shines vast;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"This describes Kaal (the Timeless) in a martial image."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਦਾੜ ਦਾੜੰ ਸੁ ਸੋਹੰ ਅਪਾਰੰ। ਜਿਨੈ ਚਰਬੀਯੰ ਜੀਵ ਜਗ੍ਯੰ ਹਜਾਰੰ। ੧੮।","roman":"Mahaa daar daaran su sohan apaaran | jinai charbeeyan jeev jagyan hajaaran | 18 |","meaning_en":"His great tusks shine boundless, which have chewed up thousands of beings of the world.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਾੜ: tusks / great teeth, an image of the all-devouring Timeless (death)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[19],"number_text":"੧੯।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਡਮਾ ਡੰਡ ਡਉਰੂ ਸਿਤਾਸੇਤ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ। ਹਾਹਾ ਹੂਹ ਹਾਸੰ ਝਮਾ ਝਮ ਅਤ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Damaa dand dauroo sitaaset chhatran | haahaa hooh haasan jhamaa jham atran |","meaning_en":"The damaru drum sounds 'dama-dand', a white and black canopy (over Him); a laugh 'ha-ha hu-hu', and His weapons flash;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਤਾਸੇਤ: read as 'white and black' (light and dark) or 'pure white'. ਅਤ੍ਰੰ: weapons (ਅਸਤ੍ਰ)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਘੋਰ ਸਬਦੰ ਬਜੇ ਸੰਖ ਐਸੰ। ਪ੍ਰਲੈ ਕਾਲ ਕੇ ਕਾਲ ਕੀ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਜੈਸੰ। ੧੯।","roman":"Mahaa ghor sabdan baje sankh aisan | pralai kaal ke kaal kee jvaal jaisan | 19 |","meaning_en":"the conch sounds with a very dreadful sound, like the flame of death at the time of dissolution (pralay).","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਲੈ ਕਾਲ: the time of the world's dissolution."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[20],"number_text":"੨੦।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਣੰ ਘੰਟ ਬਾਜੰ। ਧੁਣੰ ਮੇਘ ਲਾਜੰ।","roman":"Ghanan ghant baajan | dhunan megh laajan |","meaning_en":"Many bells ring; their sound shames the clouds (thunder);","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਯੋ ਸਦ ਏਵੰ। ਹੜਿਯੋ ਨੀਰ ਧੇਵੰ। ੨੦।","roman":"Bhayo sad evan | hariyo neer dhevan | 20 |","meaning_en":"such a sound arose, as when water surges in the ocean.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨੀਰ ਧੇਵੰ: read as 'the ocean (ਨੀਰਧਿ)'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[21],"number_text":"੨੧।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘੁਰੰ ਘੁੰਘਰੇਯੰ। ਧੁਣੰ ਨੇਵਰੇਯੰ।","roman":"Ghuran ghunghreyan | dhunan nevreyan |","meaning_en":"Ankle-bells jingle, anklets sound;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨੇਵਰ: anklets."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਨਾਦ ਨਾਦੰ। ਸੁਰੰ ਨਿਰਬਿਖਾਦੰ। ੨੧।","roman":"Mahaa naad naadan | suran nirbikhaadan | 21 |","meaning_en":"the great sound of sounds, a melody free of sorrow.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[22],"number_text":"੨੨।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰੰ ਮਾਲ ਰਾਜੰ। ਲਖੇ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਲਾਜੰ।","roman":"Siran maal raajan | lakhe rudr laajan |","meaning_en":"A garland (of skulls) adorns His head; seeing it, Rudra (Shiva) is put to shame;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਰੰ ਮਾਲ: read as a garland of heads (skulls), Shiva's own emblem, which is outdone here."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਭੇ ਚਾਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰੰ। ਪਰਮੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ। ੨੨।","roman":"Subhe chaar chitran | parman pavitran | 22 |","meaning_en":"beautiful and wondrous, supremely pure.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[23],"number_text":"੨੩।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਗਰਜ ਗਰਜੰ। ਸੁਣੇ ਦੂਤ ਲਰਜੰ।","roman":"Mahaa garaj garjan | sune doot larjan |","meaning_en":"He roars a great roar; hearing it, the messengers (of death) tremble;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੂਤ: messengers of Yama (death)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰਵੰ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਸੋਹੰ। ਮਹਾ ਮਾਨ ਮੋਹੰ। ੨੩।","roman":"Sravan sron sohan | mahaa maan mohan | 23 |","meaning_en":"streaming blood adorns Him; He enchants the pride of the great.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸ੍ਰਵੰ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ: flowing blood (of the slain enemies). ਮਹਾ ਮਾਨ ਮੋਹੰ: read as 'He bewitches (breaks) great pride'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[24],"number_text":"੨੪।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰਿਜੇ ਸੇਤਜੰ ਜੇਰਜੰ ਉਤਭੁਜੇਵੰ। ਰਚੇ ਅੰਡਜੰ ਖੰਡ ਬ੍ਰਹਮੰਡ ਏਵੰ।","roman":"Srije setjan jerjan utbhujevan | rache andjan khand brahmand evan |","meaning_en":"He created those born of sweat, of wombs and of the earth; He made those born of eggs, the regions and the universe;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਸਾ ਬਿਦਿਸਾਯੰ ਜਿਮੀ ਆਸਮਾਣੰ। ਚਤੁਰ ਬੇਦ ਕਥ੍ਯੰ ਕੁਰਾਣੰ ਪੁਰਾਣੰ। ੨੪।","roman":"Disaa bidisaayan jimee aasmaanan | chatur bed kathyan kuraanan puraanan | 24 |","meaning_en":"the directions and the intermediate directions, the earth and the sky; (He created) the four Vedas, and what the Quran and Puranas tell of.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[25],"number_text":"੨੫।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਚੇ ਰੈਣ ਦਿਵਸੰ ਥਪੇ ਸੂਰ ਚੰਦ੍ਰੰ। ਠਟੇ ਦਈਵ ਦਾਨੋ ਰਚੇ ਬੀਰ ਬਿੰਦ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Rache rain divsan thape soor chandran | thate daeev daano rache beer bindran |","meaning_en":"He made night and day, set up the sun and moon; He fashioned gods and demons and created hosts of heroes;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੀ ਲੋਹ ਕਲਮੰ ਲਿਖ੍ਯੋ ਲੇਖ ਮਾਥੰ। ਸਬੈ ਜੇਰ ਕੀਨੇ ਬਲੀ ਕਾਲ ਹਾਥੰ। ੨੫।","roman":"Karee loh kalman likhyo lekh maathan | sabai jer keene balee kaal haathan | 25 |","meaning_en":"He made an iron pen and wrote the destiny on the forehead; the mighty Kaal has brought all under His hand.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲੋਹ ਕਲਮੰ: an iron pen, i.e. an unchangeable writ of destiny."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[26],"number_text":"੨੬।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਈ ਮੇਟਿ ਡਾਰੇ ਉਸਾਰੇ ਬਨਾਏ। ਉਪਾਰੇ ਗੜੇ ਫੇਰਿ ਮੇਟੇ ਉਪਾਏ।","roman":"Kaee meti daare usaare banaae | upaare gare pheri mete upaae |","meaning_en":"Many He erased, many He raised and made; He uprooted, fashioned, and again erased and created.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਕਾਲ ਜੂ ਕੀ ਕਿਨੂ ਨ ਪਛਾਨੀ। ਘਨਿਯੋ ਪੈ ਬਿਹੈ ਹੈ ਘਨਿਯੋ ਪੈ ਬਿਹਾਨੀ। ੨੬।","roman":"Kriaa kaal joo kee kinoo na pachhaanee | ghaniyo pai bihai hai ghaniyo pai bihaanee | 26 |","meaning_en":"No one has understood the doings of Kaal; many have passed under Him and many more will pass.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘਨਿਯੋ ਪੈ ਬਿਹੈ ਹੈ ਘਨਿਯੋ ਪੈ ਬਿਹਾਨੀ: 'over many it will pass, over many it has passed', i.e. His work has gone on and will go on."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[27],"number_text":"੨੭।","page":137,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਸੇ ਕੀਟ ਕੋਟੈ ਬਨਾਏ। ਕਿਤੇ ਰਾਮ ਸੇ ਮੇਟਿ ਡਾਰੇ ਉਪਾਏ।","roman":"Kite krisan se keet kotai banaae | kite raam se meti daare upaae |","meaning_en":"He has made millions of Krishnas like worms; He created Ramas and erased them;","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Krishna and Rama are presented as created beings within the power of the Timeless."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾਦੀਨ ਕੇਤੇ ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀ ਮਾਝਿ ਹੂਏ। ਸਮੈ ਆਪਨੀ ਆਪਨੀ ਅੰਤਿ ਮੂਏ। ੨੭।","roman":"Mahaadeen kete prithee maajhi hooe | samai aapnee aapnee anti mooe | 27 |","meaning_en":"how many great Muhammads (great prophets) came upon the earth; each died at their own appointed time.","page":137,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹਾਦੀਨ: read as 'Muhammad' (as in many commentaries) or 'great men of faith'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[28],"number_text":"੨੮।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਅਉਲੀਆ ਅੰਬੀਆ ਹੋਇ ਬੀਤੇ। ਤਿਤ੍ਯੋ ਕਾਲ ਜੀਤਾ ਨ ਤੇ ਕਾਲੇ ਜੀਤੇ।","roman":"Jite auleeaa anbeeaa hoi beete | tityo kaal jeetaa na te kaale jeete |","meaning_en":"All the saints and prophets who have come and gone: none of them conquered Kaal; Kaal conquered them all.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਉਲੀਆ: Muslim saints (awliya). ਅੰਬੀਆ: prophets (anbiya). The edition prints ਕਾਲੇ, kept as printed."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਰਾਮ ਸੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਹੁਇ ਬਿਸਨੁ ਆਏ। ਤਿਤ੍ਯੋ ਕਾਲ ਖਾਪਿਓ ਨ ਤੇ ਕਾਲ ਘਾਏ। ੨੮।","roman":"Jite raam se krisan hui bisnu aae | tityo kaal khaapio na te kaal ghaae | 28 |","meaning_en":"All the Ramas, Krishnas and Vishnus who came: Kaal destroyed them all, none of them destroyed Kaal.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[29],"number_text":"੨੯।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਸੇ ਚੰਦ੍ਰ ਸੇ ਹੋਤ ਆਏ। ਤਿਤ੍ਯੋ ਕਾਲ ਖਾਪਾ ਨ ਤੇ ਕਾਲਿ ਘਾਏ।","roman":"Jite indr se chandr se hot aae | tityo kaal khaapaa na te kaali ghaae |","meaning_en":"All who came like Indra and the moon: Kaal destroyed them all, none of them destroyed Kaal.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਅਉਲੀਆ ਅੰਬੀਆ ਗਉਸ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈਂ। ਸਭੈ ਕਾਲ ਕੇ ਅੰਤ ਦਾੜਾ ਤਲੈ ਹੈ। ੨੯।","roman":"Jite auleeaa anbeeaa gaus hvai hain | sabhai kaal ke ant daaraa talai hai | 29 |","meaning_en":"All the saints, prophets and Ghauses who will be: all of them, in the end, are under Kaal's jaws.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਉਸ: a high rank of Muslim saint (ghaus)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[30],"number_text":"੩੦।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਮਾਨਧਾਤਾਦਿ ਰਾਜਾ ਸੁਹਾਏ। ਸਭੈ ਬਾਧਿ ਕੈ ਕਾਲ ਜੇਲੈ ਚਲਾਏ।","roman":"Jite maandhaataadi raajaa suhaae | sabhai baadhi kai kaal jelai chalaae |","meaning_en":"All the glorious kings like Mandhata: Kaal bound them all and drove them into His prison.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਨਧਾਤਾ: Mandhata, a legendary ancient king."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨੈ ਨਾਮ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਉਚਾਰੋ ਉਬਾਰੇ। ਬਿਨਾ ਸਾਮ ਤਾ ਕੀ ਲਖੇ ਕੋਟਿ ਮਾਰੇ। ੩੦।","roman":"Jinai naam taa ko uchaaro ubaare | binaa saam taa kee lakhe koti maare | 30 |","meaning_en":"Those who uttered His name were saved; without His protection, millions are seen destroyed.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਾਮ: refuge, protection (ਸਰਣ)."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ। ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tvaprasaadi | rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"By Your grace. Rasaaval metre.","page":138,"invocation":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ","meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[31],"number_text":"੩੧।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਮਕਹਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣੰ। ਅਭੂਤੰ ਭਯਾਣੰ। ਧੁਣੰ ਨੇਵਰਾਣੰ। ਘੁਰੰ ਘੁੰਘ੍ਰਯਾਣੰ। ੩੧।","roman":"Chamakhi kripaanan | abhootan bhayaanan | dhunan nevraanan | ghuran ghunghrayaanan | 31 |","meaning_en":"Swords flash, wondrous and fearsome; anklets sound, ankle-bells jingle.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਭੂਤੰ: wondrous, unlike anything (ਅਦਭੁਤ)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[32],"number_text":"੩੨।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਤੁਰ ਬਾਹ ਚਾਰੰ। ਨਿਜੂਟੰ ਸੁਧਾਰੰ। ਗਦਾ ਪਾਸ ਸੋਹੰ। ਜਮੰ ਮਾਨ ਮੋਹੰ। ੩੨।","roman":"Chatur baah chaaran | nijootan sudhaaran | gadaa paas sohan | jaman maan mohan | 32 |","meaning_en":"Four beautiful arms, the matted hair well tied; the mace and the noose shine, enchanting even the pride of Yama.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਜੂਟੰ: matted hair (ਜੂੜਾ / ਜਟਾ). ਜਮੰ ਮਾਨ ਮੋਹੰ: humbling even Yama (death)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[33],"number_text":"੩੩।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਭੰ ਜੀਭ ਜੁਆਲੰ। ਸੁ ਦਾੜਾ ਕਰਾਲੰ। ਬਜੀ ਬੰਬ ਸੰਖੰ। ਉਠੇ ਨਾਦੰ ਬੰਖੰ। ੩੩।","roman":"Subhan jeebh juaalan | su daaraa karaalan | bajee banb sankhan | uthe naadan bankhan | 33 |","meaning_en":"The tongue (a flame of fire) shines, the tusks are fearsome; the bugle and conch sound, and the war-trumpet's roar rises.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੰਬ: war-drum / bugle. ਬੰਖ: read as 'trumpet'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[34],"number_text":"੩੪।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਭੰ ਰੂਪ ਸਿਆਮੰ। ਮਹਾ ਸੋਭ ਧਾਮੰ। ਛਬੇ ਚਾਰੁ ਚਿੰਤ੍ਰੰ। ਪਰੇਅੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰੰ। ੩੪।","roman":"Subhan roop siaaman | mahaa sobh dhaaman | chhabe chaaru chintran | parean pavitran | 34 |","meaning_en":"Beautiful, dark in form, the abode of great splendour; wondrous in beauty, beyond all, pure.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਆਮੰ: dark (blue-black) in colour."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[35],"number_text":"੩੫।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰੰ ਸੇਤ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ ਸੁ ਸੁਭ੍ਰੰ ਬਿਰਾਜੰ। ਲਖੇ ਛੈਲ ਛਾਇਆ ਕਰੇ ਤੇਜ ਲਾਜੰ।","roman":"Siran set chhatran su subhran biraajan | lakhe chhail chhaaiaa kare tej laajan |","meaning_en":"A white canopy, pure and bright, shines over His head; seeing its shade, even radiance itself is ashamed;","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛੈਲ: read as 'handsome / splendid'. ਛਾਇਆ: the shade (of the canopy)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਸਾਲ ਲਾਲ ਨੈਨੰ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ ਸੋਹੰ। ਢਿਗੰ ਅੰਸੁਮਾਲੰ ਹਸੰ ਕੋਟਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਹੰ। ੩੫।","roman":"Bisaal laal nainan mahaaraaj sohan | dhigan ansumaalan hasan koti krohan | 35 |","meaning_en":"His large red eyes shine, O great King; beside them, millions of suns, in their brilliance, are put to shame.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਸੁਮਾਲ: the sun ('garlanded with rays'). ਹਸੰ ਕੋਟਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਹੰ: read as 'millions (of suns) are laughed at / outshone'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[36],"number_text":"੩੬।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰੇ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ ਸੋਹੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਦੇਵ ਕੰਨਿਆਨਿ ਕੇ ਮਾਨ ਮੋਹੰ।","roman":"Kahoon roop dhaare mahaaraaj sohan | kahoon dev kanniaani ke maan mohan |","meaning_en":"Somewhere He shines, taking the form of a great king; somewhere He enchants the pride of divine maidens;","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਬੀਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੇ ਧਰੇ ਬਾਨ ਪਾਨੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਭੂਪ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ ਬਜਾਏ ਨਿਸਾਨੰ। ੩੬।","roman":"Kahoon beer hvai ke dhare baan paanan | kahoon bhoop hvai kai bajaae nisaanan | 36 |","meaning_en":"somewhere, as a hero, He holds the arrow in His hand; somewhere, as a king, He sounds the war-drum.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸਾਨ: kettle-drum, a royal emblem."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[37],"number_text":"੩੭।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਨੁਰ ਬਾਨ ਧਾਰੇ। ਛਕੇ ਛੈਲ ਭਾਰੇ।","roman":"Dhanur baan dhaare | chhake chhail bhaare |","meaning_en":"Holding the bow and arrow, handsome and mighty;","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਏ ਖਗ ਐਸੇ। ਮਹਾਬੀਰ ਜੈਸੇ। ੩੭।","roman":"Lae khag aise | mahaabeer jaise | 37 |","meaning_en":"He holds the sword like a great hero.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[38],"number_text":"੩੮।","page":138,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਰੇ ਜੰਗ ਜੋਰੰ। ਕਰੇ ਜੁਧ ਘੋਰੰ।","roman":"Jure jang joran | kare judh ghoran |","meaning_en":"He joins battle with force and wages a dreadful war;","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾ ਨਿਧਿ ਦਿਆਲੰ। ਸਦਾਯੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਲੰ। ੩੮।","roman":"Kripaa nidhi diaalan | sadaayan kripaalan | 38 |","meaning_en":"yet He is the merciful treasure of grace, ever compassionate.","page":138,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[39],"number_text":"੩੯।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਦਾ ਏਕ ਰੂਪੰ। ਸਭੈ ਲੋਕ ਭੂਪੰ।","roman":"Sadaa ek roopan | sabhai lok bhoopan |","meaning_en":"Ever of one form, King of all the worlds;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਜੇਅੰ ਅਜਾਯੰ। ਸਰਨਿਯੰ ਸਹਾਯੰ। ੩੯।","roman":"Ajean ajaayan | sarniyan sahaayan | 39 |","meaning_en":"unconquerable, unborn, helper of those who seek refuge.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[40],"number_text":"੪੦।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਪੈ ਖਗ ਪਾਨੰ। ਮਹਾ ਲੋਕ ਦਾਨੰ।","roman":"Tapai khag paanan | mahaa lok daanan |","meaning_en":"The sword shines in His hand; He is the great Giver to the worlds;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵਿਖਿਅੰ ਭਵੇਅੰ। ਨਮੋ ਨਿਰਜੁਰੇਅੰ। ੪੦।","roman":"Bhavikhian bhavean | namo nirjurean | 40 |","meaning_en":"He is in the future and the present; salutation to the One free of affliction.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[41],"number_text":"੪੧।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਧੋ ਮਾਨ ਮੁੰਡੰ। ਸੁਭੰ ਰੁੰਡ ਝੁੰਡੰ।","roman":"Madho maan mundan | subhan rund jhundan |","meaning_en":"He crushes the pride of Madhu and Mundh; (with Him) are throngs of headless trunks;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਧੋ, ਮੁੰਡੰ: the demons Madhu and Mundh; ਰੁੰਡ: headless trunks on the battlefield. The line is read in several ways."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰੰ ਸੇਤ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ। ਲਸੰ ਹਾਥ ਅਤ੍ਰੰ। ੪੧।","roman":"Siran set chhatran | lasan haath atran | 41 |","meaning_en":"a white canopy over His head, weapons shining in His hand.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[42],"number_text":"੪੨।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣੇ ਨਾਦ ਭਾਰੀ। ਤ੍ਰਸੈ ਛਤ੍ਰਧਾਰੀ।","roman":"Sune naad bhaaree | trasai chhatradhaaree |","meaning_en":"Hearing His mighty sound, the canopied kings tremble;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਸਾ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਰਾਜੰ। ਸੁਣੇ ਦੋਖ ਭਾਜੰ। ੪੨।","roman":"Disaa basatr raajan | sune dokh bhaajan | 42 |","meaning_en":"the directions are His robe; hearing (of Him), sins run away.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਸਾ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ: clothed in the directions (the sky), like Shiva. ਦੋਖ: faults, sins."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[43],"number_text":"੪੩।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣੇ ਗਦ ਸਦੰ। ਅਨੰਤੰ ਬੇਹਦੰ।","roman":"Sune gad sadan | anantan behdan |","meaning_en":"Hearing His joyful sound, (He is known as) infinite and without limit;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਦ ਸਦੰ: read as 'the sound of rejoicing'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟਾ ਜਾਣੁ ਸਿਆਮੰ। ਦੁਤੰ ਅਭਿਰਾਮੰ। ੪੩।","roman":"Ghataa jaanu siaaman | dutan abhiraaman | 43 |","meaning_en":"dark like a cloud, of delightful splendour.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[44],"number_text":"੪੪।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਤੁਰ ਬਾਹ ਚਾਰੰ। ਕਰੀਟੰ ਸੁਧਾਰੰ।","roman":"Chatur baah chaaran | kareetan sudhaaran |","meaning_en":"Four beautiful arms, a crown well arranged;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਦਾ ਸੰਖ ਚਕ੍ਰੰ। ਦਿਪੈ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਬਕ੍ਰੰ। ੪੪।","roman":"Gadaa sankh chakran | dipai kroor bakran | 44 |","meaning_en":"the mace, conch and discus shine, fearsome and bent (curved).","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Mace, conch and discus are Vishnu's emblems; here they are attributes of the Timeless."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraaj metre.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[45],"number_text":"੪੫।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨੂਪ ਰੂਪ ਰਾਜਿਅੰ। ਨਿਹਾਰ ਕਾਮ ਲਾਜਿਯੰ।","roman":"Anoop roop raajian | nihaar kaam laajiyan |","meaning_en":"His incomparable form shines; seeing it, Kaam (the god of love) is ashamed;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਲੋਕ ਲੋਕ ਸੋਭਿਅੰ। ਬਿਲੋਕ ਲੋਕ ਲੋਭਿਅੰ। ੪੫।","roman":"Alok lok sobhian | bilok lok lobhian | 45 |","meaning_en":"His unseen splendour adorns the worlds; seeing it, the worlds are filled with longing.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[46],"number_text":"੪੬।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਮਕਿ ਚੰਦ੍ਰ ਸੀਸਿਯੰ। ਰਹਿਯੋ ਲਜਾਇ ਈਸਯੰ।","roman":"Chamki chandr seesiyan | rahiyo lajaai eesyan |","meaning_en":"The moon gleams on His head; Ish (Shiva) is put to shame;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Shiva wears the crescent moon on his head."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਸੋਭ ਨਾਗ ਭੂਖੰਣੰ। ਅਨੇਕ ਦੁਸਟ ਦੂਖਣੰ। ੪੬।","roman":"Su sobh naag bhookhannan | anek dusat dookhnan | 46 |","meaning_en":"the serpent-ornaments shine beautifully, the tormentors of many wicked ones.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[47],"number_text":"੪੭।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਪਾਣ ਧਾਰੀਯੰ। ਕਰੋਰ ਪਾਪ ਟਾਰੀਯੰ।","roman":"Kripaan paan dhaareeyan | karor paap taareeyan |","meaning_en":"He holds the sword in His hand and removes millions of sins;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਦਾ ਗ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਪਾਣਿਯੰ। ਕਮਾਣ ਬਾਣ ਤਾਣਿਯੰ। ੪੭।","roman":"Gadaa grisat paaniyan | kamaan baan taaniyan | 47 |","meaning_en":"He holds the heavy mace in His hand, and draws the bow and arrow.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗ੍ਰਿਸਟ: heavy / mighty."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[48],"number_text":"੪੮।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬਦ ਸੰਖ ਬਜਿਯੰ। ਘਣੰਕਿ ਘੁੰਮਰ ਗਜਿਯੰ।","roman":"Sabad sankh bajiyan | ghananki ghunmar gajiyan |","meaning_en":"The sound of the conch rings out, and roars like thunderclouds;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਨਿ ਨਾਥ ਤੋਰੀਯੰ। ਉਬਾਰ ਲਾਜ ਮੋਰੀਯੰ। ੪੮।","roman":"Sarni naath toreeyan | ubaar laaj moreeyan | 48 |","meaning_en":"O Lord, I am in Your refuge; save my honour.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[49],"number_text":"੪੯।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨੇਕ ਰੂਪ ਸੋਹੀਯੰ। ਬਿਸੇਖ ਦੇਵ ਮੋਹੀਯੰ।","roman":"Anek roop soheeyan | bisekh dev moheeyan |","meaning_en":"He shines in many forms, and enchants even the special gods;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਦੇਵ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵਲੰ। ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾ ਨਿਧਾਨ ਕੇਵਲੰ। ੪੯।","roman":"Adev dev devlan | kripaa nidhaan kevlan | 49 |","meaning_en":"the God of demons and gods; He alone is the treasure of mercy.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੇਵਲੰ: read as 'the god (ਦੇਵ)' or 'the temple'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[50],"number_text":"੫੦।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਆਦਿ ਅੰਤਿ ਏਕਿਯੰ। ਧਰੇ ਸਰੂਪ ਅਨੇਕਿਯੰ।","roman":"Su aadi anti ekiyan | dhare saroop anekiyan |","meaning_en":"In the beginning and the end He is One, having taken many forms;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਪਾਣ ਰਾਜਈ। ਬਿਲੋਕ ਪਾਪ ਭਾਜਈ। ੫੦।","roman":"Kripaan paan raajaee | bilok paap bhaajaee | 50 |","meaning_en":"the sword shines in His hand; seeing it, sin runs away.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[51],"number_text":"੫੧।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਲੰਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਸੁ ਦੇਹਯੰ। ਤਨੋ ਮਨੋ ਕਿ ਮੋਹਿਯੰ।","roman":"Alankrit su dehyan | tano mano ki mohiyan |","meaning_en":"His body is beautifully adorned, as if body and mind were enchanted;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਮਾਣ ਬਾਣ ਧਾਰਹੀ। ਅਨੇਕ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਟਾਰਹੀ। ੫੧।","roman":"Kamaan baan dhaarhee | anek satr taarhee | 51 |","meaning_en":"He holds the bow and arrow, and destroys many enemies.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[52],"number_text":"੫੨।","page":139,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਮਕਿ ਘੁੰਘਰੰ ਸੁਰੰ। ਨਵੰ ਨਨਾਦ ਨੂਪਰੰ।","roman":"Ghamki ghunghran suran | navan nanaad noopran |","meaning_en":"The ankle-bells ring with sound, the new anklets jingle;","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਜੁਆਲ ਬਿਜੁਲੰ ਜੁਲੰ। ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰ ਪਰਮ ਨਿਰਮਲੰ। ੫੨।","roman":"Prajuaal bijulan julan | pavitr param niramlan | 52 |","meaning_en":"He blazes like lightning, pure, supremely spotless.","page":139,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤੋਟਕ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ। ਤੋਟਕ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tvaprasaadi | totak chhand","meaning_en":"By Your grace. Totak metre.","page":140,"invocation":"ਤ੍ਵਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ","meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[53],"number_text":"੫੩।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਵ ਨੇਵਰ ਨਾਦ ਸੁਰੰ ਨ੍ਰਿਮਲੰ। ਮੁਖ ਬਿਜੁਲ ਜੁਆਲ ਘਣੰ ਪ੍ਰਜੁਲੰ।","roman":"Nav nevar naad suran nrimlan | mukh bijul juaal ghanan prajulan |","meaning_en":"The new anklets give a clear sound; from His mouth the flame of lightning blazes like a cloud;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨ੍ਰਿਮਲੰ: clear, pure."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਦਰਾ ਕਰ ਮਤ ਮਹਾ ਭਭਕੰ। ਬਨ ਮੈ ਮਨੋ ਬਾਘ ਬਚਾ ਬਬਕੰ। ੫੩।","roman":"Madraa kar mat mahaa bhabhkan | ban mai mano baagh bachaa babkan | 53 |","meaning_en":"as if drunk with wine He roars loudly, like a tiger's cub growling in the forest.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The image is of the fierce, joyful might of the Timeless in battle."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[54],"number_text":"੫੪।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵ ਭੂਤ ਭਵਿਖ ਭਵਾਨ ਭਵੰ। ਕਲ ਕਾਰਣ ਉਬਾਰਣ ਏਕ ਤੁਵੰ।","roman":"Bhav bhoot bhavikh bhavaan bhavan | kal kaaran ubaaran ek tuvan |","meaning_en":"In the world, past, future and present, You alone are the cause and the saviour (in this age);","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲ ਕਾਰਣ: read as 'the cause of power / of all' or 'in the Kali age'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਠੌਰ ਨਿਰੰਤਰ ਨਿਤ ਨਯੰ। ਮ੍ਰਿਦ ਮੰਗਲ ਰੂਪ ਤੁਯੰ ਸੁਭਯੰ। ੫੪।","roman":"Sabh thaur nirantar nit nayan | mrid mangal roop tuyan subhyan | 54 |","meaning_en":"in every place, constantly and always, Your form is gentle, joyful and auspicious.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਤ ਨਯੰ: read as 'ever new' or 'always'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[55],"number_text":"੫੫।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦ੍ਰਿੜ ਦਾੜ ਕਰਾਲ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਸੇਤ ਉਧੰ। ਜਿਹ ਭਾਜਤ ਦੁਸਟ ਬਿਲੋਕ ਜੁਧੰ।","roman":"Drir daar karaal dvai set udhan | jih bhaajat dusat bilok judhan |","meaning_en":"Strong, fearsome tusks, two white ones rising; seeing them in battle the wicked flee;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਦ ਮਤ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਕਰਾਲ ਧਰੰ। ਜਯ ਸਦ ਸੁਰਾਸੁਰਯੰ ਉਚਰੰ। ੫੫।","roman":"Mad mat kripaan karaal dharan | jay sad suraasuryan uchran | 55 |","meaning_en":"intoxicated (with battle), He holds the fearsome sword; gods and demons cry 'victory'.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[56],"number_text":"੫੬।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਵ ਕਿੰਕਣ ਨੇਵਰ ਨਾਦ ਹੂੰਅੰ। ਚਲ ਚਾਲ ਸਭਾਚਲ ਕੰਪ ਭੂਅੰ।","roman":"Nav kinkan nevar naad hoonan | chal chaal sabhaachal kanp bhooan |","meaning_en":"New girdle-bells and anklets sound; as He moves, the mountains and the earth tremble;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਿੰਕਣ: small bells on a girdle. ਸਭਾਚਲ: all the mountains."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਣ ਘੁੰਘਰ ਘੰਟਣ ਘੋਰ ਸੁਰੰ। ਚਰ ਚਾਰ ਚਰਾਚਰਯੰ ਹੁਹਰੰ। ੫੬।","roman":"Ghan ghunghar ghantan ghor suran | char chaar charaacharyan huhran | 56 |","meaning_en":"many ankle-bells and bells ring with a dreadful sound; all moving and unmoving things are stirred.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਰਾਚਰ: the moving and the unmoving (all creation). ਹੁਹਰੰ: read as 'shaken / startled'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[57],"number_text":"੫੭।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲ ਚੌਦਹੂੰ ਚਕ੍ਰਨ ਚਕ੍ਰ ਫਿਰੰ। ਬਢਵੰ ਘਟਵੰ ਹਰੀਅੰ ਸੁਭਰੰ।","roman":"Chal chaudhoon chakran chakr phiran | badhvan ghatvan hareean subhran |","meaning_en":"His discus turns through the fourteen worlds; He increases and decreases, destroys and fills;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਕ੍ਰ: discus / wheel (of command)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਜੀਵ ਜਿਤੇ ਜਲਯੰ ਥਲਯੰ। ਅਸ ਕੋ ਜੁ ਤਵਾਇਸਿਅੰ ਮਲਯੰ। ੫੭।","roman":"Jag jeev jite jalyan thalyan | as ko ju tavaaisian malyan | 57 |","meaning_en":"of all the beings of the world, in water and on land, who is there who can erase Your command?","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਵਾਇਸਿਅੰ: Your command (ਆਇਸੁ). ਮਲਯੰ: read as 'can crush / erase'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[58],"number_text":"੫੮।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟ ਭਾਦਵ ਮਾਸ ਕੀ ਜਾਣ ਸੁੰਭ। ਤਨ ਸਾਵਰੇ ਰਾਵਰੇਅੰ ਹੁਲਸੰ।","roman":"Ghat bhaadav maas kee jaan sunbh | tan saavre raavrean hulsan |","meaning_en":"He is beautiful like a cloud of the month of Bhadon; His dark body is joyful;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"This edition prints ਸੁੰਭ without its ending (the usual reading is ਸੁਭੰ, beautiful)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਦ ਪੰਗਤਿ ਦਾਮਿਨੀਅੰ ਦਮੰਕੰ। ਘਟ ਘੁੰਘਰ ਘੰਟ ਸੁਰ ਘਮਕੰ। ੫੮।","roman":"Rad pangti daamineean damankan | ghat ghunghar ghant sur ghamkan | 58 |","meaning_en":"His rows of teeth flash like lightning; the ankle-bells and bells sound and ring.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਾਮਿਨੀ: lightning."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[59],"number_text":"੫੯।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟਾ ਸਾਵਣੰ ਜਾਣ ਸ੍ਯਾਮੰ ਸੁਹਾਯੰ। ਮਣੀ ਨੀਲ ਨਗਿਯੰ ਲਖ ਸੀਸ ਨਿਆਯੰ।","roman":"Ghataa saavnan jaan syaaman suhaayan | manee neel nagiyan lakh sees niaayan |","meaning_en":"Dark and beautiful like a cloud of Saavan; seeing Him, sapphires and gems bow their heads;","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਣੀ ਨੀਲ: sapphire. Saavan: the rainy month."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਸ੍ਯਾਮੰ ਮਹਾ ਅਭਿਰਾਮੰ। ਮਹਾ ਰੂਪ ਰੂਪੰ ਮਹਾ ਕਾਮ ਕਾਮੰ। ੫੯।","roman":"Mahaa sundar syaaman mahaa abhiraaman | mahaa roop roopan mahaa kaam kaaman | 59 |","meaning_en":"very beautiful, dark, very charming, the Form of great forms, the Love of great loves.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[60],"number_text":"੬੦।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰੈ ਚਕ੍ਰ ਚਉਦਹ ਪੁਰੀਯੰ ਮਧਿਆਣੰ। ਇਸੋ ਕੌਨ ਬੀਯੰ ਫਿਰੈ ਆਇਸਾਣੰ।","roman":"Phirai chakr chaudah pureeyan madhiaanan | iso kaun beeyan phirai aaisaanan |","meaning_en":"His discus turns amid the fourteen worlds; who else is there who can go against His command?","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਫਿਰੈ ਆਇਸਾਣੰ: turns away from (disobeys) the command."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੋ ਕੁੰਟ ਕੌਨੇ ਬਿਖੈ ਭਾਜ ਬਾਚੇ। ਸਭੰ ਸੀਸ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਾਲ ਨਾਚੈ। ੬੦।","roman":"Kaho kunt kaune bikhai bhaaj baache | sabhan sees ke sang sree kaal naachai | 60 |","meaning_en":"Say, in which direction or corner can one run and be saved? Over every head the revered Kaal dances.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁੰਟ ਕੌਨੇ: direction and corner."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[61],"number_text":"੬੧।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੇ ਕੋਟ ਕੋਊ ਧਰੈ ਕੋਟਿ ਓਟੰ। ਬਚੈਗੋ ਨ ਕਿਉ ਹੂੰ ਕਰੈ ਕਾਲ ਚੋਟੰ।","roman":"Kare kot ko'oo dharai koti otan | bachaigo na kiu hoon karai kaal chotan |","meaning_en":"One may build forts and take millions of shelters, yet none will be saved when Kaal strikes.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਿਖ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੇਤੇ ਪੜੰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੋਟੰ। ਬਿਨਾ ਸਰਨਿ ਤਾਕੀ ਨਹੀ ਓਰ ਓਟੰ। ੬੧।","roman":"Likh jantr kete paran mantr kotan | binaa sarni taakee nahee or otan | 61 |","meaning_en":"How many yantras are written, millions of mantras recited: without His refuge there is no other shelter.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[62],"number_text":"੬੨।","page":140,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਿਖੰ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਥਾਕੇ ਪੜੰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਹਾਰੈ। ਕਰੇ ਕਾਲ ਕੇ ਅੰਤ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਬਿਚਾਰੇ।","roman":"Likhan jantr thaake paran mantr haarai | kare kaal ke ant lai ke bichaare |","meaning_en":"Writing yantras they grew weary, reciting mantras they lost; thinking it over, they are taken in the end by Kaal.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰੇ ਕਾਲ ਕੇ ਅੰਤ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਬਿਚਾਰੇ: read as 'in the end, the poor wretches were made Kaal's'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤਿਓ ਤੰਤ੍ਰ ਸਾਧੇ ਜੁ ਜਨਮ ਬਿਤਾਇਓ। ਭਏ ਫੋਕਟੰ ਕਾਜ ਏਕੈ ਨ ਆਇਓ। ੬੨।","roman":"Kitio tantr saadhe ju janam bitaaio | bhae phoktan kaaj ekai na aaio | 62 |","meaning_en":"How many practised tantras and spent their lives: it was all in vain, not one thing was of use.","page":140,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[63],"number_text":"੬੩।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਨਾਸ ਮੂੰਦੇ ਭਏ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਚਾਰੀ। ਕਿਤੇ ਕੰਠ ਕੰਠੀ ਜਟਾ ਸੀਸ ਧਾਰੀ।","roman":"Kite naas moonde bhae brahamchaaree | kite kanth kanthee jataa sees dhaaree |","meaning_en":"Some closed their nostrils (in breath control) and became celibates; some wore rosaries round their necks and matted hair on their heads;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੰਠੀ: a necklace / rosary of beads."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਚੀਰ ਕਾਨੰ ਜੁਗੀਸੰ ਕਹਾਯੰ। ਸਭੇ ਫੋਕਟੰ ਧਰਮ ਕਾਮੰ ਨ ਆਯੰ। ੬੩।","roman":"Kite cheer kaanan jugeesan kahaayan | sabhe phoktan dharam kaaman na aayan | 63 |","meaning_en":"some split their ears and were called great yogis; all these are empty religions, of no use.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚੀਰ ਕਾਨੰ: split ears, as worn by Nath (Kanphat) yogis."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[64],"number_text":"੬੪।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਧੁ ਕੀਟਭੰ ਰਾਛਸੇਸੰ ਬਲੀਅੰ। ਸਮੇ ਆਪਨੀ ਕਾਲ ਤੇਊ ਦਲੀਅੰ।","roman":"Madhu keetbhan raachhsesan baleean | same aapnee kaal teoo daleean |","meaning_en":"Madhu and Kaitabh, the mighty demon-kings: in their own time, Kaal crushed them too.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਧੁ ਕੀਟਭੰ: the demons Madhu and Kaitabh."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਏ ਸੁੰਭ ਨੈਸੁੰਭ ਸ੍ਰੋਣੰਤਬੀਜੰ। ਤੇਊ ਕਾਲ ਕੀਨੇ ਪੁਰੇਜੇ ਪੁਰੇਜੰ। ੬੪।","roman":"Bhae sunbh naisunbh sronantbeejan | teoo kaal keene pureje purejan | 64 |","meaning_en":"There were Sumbh, Nisumbh and Sronatbij: Kaal cut them, too, into pieces.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸ੍ਰੋਣੰਤਬੀਜ: Raktabij, the demon from whose drops of blood more demons arose. ਪੁਰੇਜੇ ਪੁਰੇਜੰ: piece by piece."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[65],"number_text":"੬੫।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਲੀ ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀਅੰ ਮਾਨਧਾਤਾ ਮਹੀਪੰ। ਜਿਨੈ ਰਥ ਚਕ੍ਰੰ ਕੀਏ ਸਾਤ ਦੀਪੰ।","roman":"Balee pritheean maandhaataa maheepan | jinai rath chakran kee'e saat deepan |","meaning_en":"Prithu the mighty, Mandhata the king of the earth, whose chariot wheels marked out the seven continents;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀ: Prithu, a legendary king. ਸਾਤ ਦੀਪ: the seven continents."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰ ਭੀਮ ਭਰਥੰ ਜਗੰ ਜੀਤ ਡੰਡਿਯੰ। ਤਿਨੈ ਅੰਤ ਕੇ ਅੰਤ ਕੌ ਕਾਲ ਖੰਡਿਯੰ। ੬੫।","roman":"Bhujan bheem bharthan jagan jeet dandiyan | tinai ant ke ant kau kaal khandiyan | 65 |","meaning_en":"Bhim of mighty arms, Bharat, who conquered and ruled the world: in the end, Kaal destroyed them.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[66],"number_text":"੬੬।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨੈ ਦੀਪ ਦੀਪੰ ਦੁਹਾਈ ਫਿਰਾਈ। ਭੁਜਾ ਦੰਡ ਦੈ ਛੋਣਿ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ ਛਿਨਾਈ।","roman":"Jinai deep deepan duhaaee phiraaee | bhujaa dand dai chhoni chhatran chhinaaee |","meaning_en":"Those whose proclamation went round every continent, who by the might of their arms seized the canopies (crowns) of the earth;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੁਹਾਈ: royal proclamation. ਛੋਣਿ: the earth."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੇ ਜਗ ਕੋਟੰ ਜਸੰ ਅਨਿਕ ਲੀਤੇ। ਵਹੈ ਬੀਰ ਬੰਕੇ ਬਲੀ ਕਾਲ ਜੀਤੇ। ੬੬।","roman":"Kare jag kotan jasan anik leete | vahai beer banke balee kaal jeete | 66 |","meaning_en":"who performed millions of sacrifices and won great fame: even those fine, mighty heroes, Kaal conquered.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[67],"number_text":"੬੭।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਈ ਕੋਟ ਲੀਨੇ ਜਿਨੈ ਦੁਰਗ ਢਾਹੇ। ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਰਬੀਰਾਨ ਕੇ ਸੈਨ ਗਾਹੇ।","roman":"Kaee kot leene jinai durag dhaahe | kite soorbeeraan ke sain gaahe |","meaning_en":"Those who took many forts and pulled down strongholds, who trampled the armies of heroes;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਈ ਜੰਗ ਕੀਨੇ ਸੁ ਸਾਕੇ ਪਵਾਰੇ। ਵਹੈ ਦੀਨ ਦੇਖੈ ਗਿਰੇ ਕਾਲ ਮਾਰੇ। ੬੭।","roman":"Kaee jang keene su saake pavaare | vahai deen dekhai gire kaal maare | 67 |","meaning_en":"who fought many wars, famous battles and ballads: even they were seen to fall, humbled, struck down by Kaal.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਾਕੇ ਪਵਾਰੇ: famous deeds and ballads (of heroism). ਦੀਨ: helpless, humbled."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[68],"number_text":"੬੮।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨੈ ਪਾਤਿਸਾਹੀ ਕਰੀ ਕੋਟਿ ਜੁਗਿਯੰ। ਰਸੰ ਆਨਰਸੰ ਭਲੀ ਭਾਤਿ ਭੁਗਿਯੰ।","roman":"Jinai paatisaahee karee koti jugiyan | rasan aanarsan bhalee bhaati bhugiyan |","meaning_en":"Those who ruled for millions of ages, and enjoyed every pleasure to the full;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਸੰ ਆਨਰਸੰ: pleasures of every kind."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਹੈ ਅੰਤ ਕੋ ਪਾਵ ਨਾਗੇ ਪਧਾਰੇ। ਗਿਰੇ ਦੀਨ ਦੇਖੇ ਹਠੀ ਕਾਲ ਮਾਰੇ। ੬੮।","roman":"Vahai ant ko paav naage padhaare | gire deen dekhe hathee kaal maare | 68 |","meaning_en":"in the end even they went barefoot; they were seen to fall, humbled, struck down by the relentless Kaal.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[69],"number_text":"੬੯।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨੈ ਖੰਡੀਅੰ ਦੰਡ ਧਾਰੰ ਅਪਾਰੰ। ਕਰੇ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਮਾ ਸੂਰ ਚੇਰੇ ਦੁਆਰੰ।","roman":"Jinai khandeean dand dhaaran apaaran | kare chandramaa soor chere duaaran |","meaning_en":"Those who broke countless rulers, who made the moon and sun servants at their door;","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੰਡ ਧਾਰ: those who wield the rod (rulers)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨੈ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਸੇ ਜੀਤ ਕੇ ਛੋਡਿ ਡਾਰੇ। ਵਹੈ ਦੀਨ ਦੇਖੇ ਗਿਰੇ ਕਾਲ ਮਾਰੇ। ੬੯।","roman":"Jinai indr se jeet ke chhodi daare | vahai deen dekhe gire kaal maare | 69 |","meaning_en":"who conquered the likes of Indra and let them go: even they were seen to fall, humbled, struck down by Kaal.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[70],"number_text":"੭੦।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਰਾਮ ਹੁਏ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤਿ ਮੂਏ। ਜਿਤੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ੭੦।","roman":"Jite raam hue | sabhai anti mooe | jite krisan hvai hai | sabhai anti jai hai | 70 |","meaning_en":"All the Ramas who have been, all died in the end; all the Krishnas who will be, all will go in the end.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[71],"number_text":"੭੧।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਦੇਵ ਹੋਸੀ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤ ਜਾਸੀ। ਜਿਤੇ ਬੋਧ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਹੈ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤਿ ਛੈ ਹੈ। ੭੧।","roman":"Jite dev hosee | sabhai ant jaasee | jite bodh hvai hai | sabhai anti chhai hai | 71 |","meaning_en":"All the gods who will be, all will go in the end; all the Buddhas who will be, all will perish in the end.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੋਧ: Buddhas (enlightened ones)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[72],"number_text":"੭੨।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਦੇਵ ਰਾਯੰ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤ ਜਾਯੰ। ਜਿਤੇ ਦਈਤ ਏਸੰ। ਤਿਤ੍ਯੋ ਕਾਲ ਲੇਸੰ। ੭੨।","roman":"Jite dev raayan | sabhai ant jaayan | jite daeet esan | tityo kaal lesan | 72 |","meaning_en":"All the kings of the gods, all will go in the end; all the lords of the demons, Kaal will take them all.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[73],"number_text":"੭੩।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰਸਿੰਘਾਵਤਾਰੰ। ਵਹੇ ਕਾਲ ਮਾਰੰ। ਬਡੋ ਡੰਡਧਾਰੀ। ਹਣਿਓ ਕਾਲ ਭਾਰੀ। ੭੩।","roman":"Narsinghaavtaaran | vahe kaal maaran | bado danddhaaree | hanio kaal bhaaree | 73 |","meaning_en":"The Narsingh incarnation: him too Kaal struck down; the great wielder of the rod, mighty Kaal slew him.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਰਸਿੰਘ: the man-lion incarnation of Vishnu. ਡੰਡਧਾਰੀ: read as Narsingh or Yama; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[74],"number_text":"੭੪।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਜੰ ਬਾਵਨੇਯੰ। ਹਣਿਯੋ ਕਾਲ ਤੇਯੰ। ਮਹਾ ਮਛ ਮੁੰਡੰ। ਫਧਿਓ ਕਾਲ ਝੁੰਡੰ। ੭੪।","roman":"Dijan baavneyan | haniyo kaal teyan | mahaa machh mundan | phadhio kaal jhundan | 74 |","meaning_en":"The Brahmin Vamana, him too Kaal slew; the great Fish (incarnation), Kaal caught in His net.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਵਨ: the dwarf incarnation. ਮਛ: the fish incarnation. ਫਧਿਓ ... ਝੁੰਡੰ: read as 'trapped in the net'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[75],"number_text":"੭੫।","page":141,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਹੋਇ ਬੀਤੇ। ਤਿਤੇ ਕਾਲ ਜੀਤੇ। ਜਿਤੇ ਸਰਨਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ਤਿਤਿਓ ਰਾਖਿ ਲੈਹੇ। ੭੫।","roman":"Jite hoi beete | tite kaal jeete | jite sarni jai hai | titio raakhi laihe | 75 |","meaning_en":"All who have been and gone, Kaal has conquered them all; all who go to His refuge, He will keep safe.","page":141,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[76],"number_text":"੭੬।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਨਾ ਸਰਨਿ ਤਾਕੀ ਨ ਅਉਰੈ ਉਪਾਯੰ। ਕਹਾ ਦੇਵ ਦਈਤੰ ਕਹਾ ਰੰਕ ਰਾਯੰ।","roman":"Binaa sarni taakee na aurai upaayan | kahaa dev daeetan kahaa rank raayan |","meaning_en":"Without His refuge there is no other way; what are gods and demons, what are paupers and kings?","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਾ ਪਾਤਿਸਾਹੰ ਕਹਾ ਉਮਰਾਯੰ। ਬਿਨਾ ਸਰਨਿ ਤਾਕੀ ਨ ਕੋਟੈ ਉਪਾਯੰ। ੭੬।","roman":"Kahaa paatisaahan kahaa umraayan | binaa sarni taakee na kotai upaayan | 76 |","meaning_en":"What are emperors, what are nobles? Without His refuge, millions of efforts are of no use.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਮਰਾਯ: nobles (umara)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[77],"number_text":"੭੭।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਜੀਵ ਜੰਤੰ ਸੁ ਦੁਨੀਅੰ ਉਪਾਯੰ। ਸਭੈ ਅੰਤਿਕਾਲੰ ਬਲੀ ਕਾਲਿ ਘਾਯੰ।","roman":"Jite jeev jantan su duneean upaayan | sabhai antikaalan balee kaali ghaayan |","meaning_en":"All the beings and creatures created in the world, at the final hour mighty Kaal destroys them all.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਨਾ ਸਰਨਿ ਤਾਕੀ ਨਹੀ ਔਰ ਓਟੰ। ਲਿਖੇ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੇਤੇ ਪੜੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੋਟੰ। ੭੭।","roman":"Binaa sarni taakee nahee aur otan | likhe jantr kete pare mantr kotan | 77 |","meaning_en":"Without His refuge there is no other shelter, however many yantras are written and millions of mantras recited.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraaj metre.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[78],"number_text":"੭੮।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇਕਿ ਰਾਜ ਰੰਕਯੰ। ਹਨੇ ਸੁ ਕਾਲ ਬੰਕਯੰ।","roman":"Jiteki raaj rankyan | hane su kaal bankyan |","meaning_en":"All the kings and paupers, the mighty Kaal has slain;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇਕਿ ਲੋਕ ਪਾਲਯੰ। ਨਿਦਾਨ ਕਾਲ ਦਾਲਯੰ। ੭੮।","roman":"Jiteki lok paalyan | nidaan kaal daalyan | 78 |","meaning_en":"all the guardians of the worlds, in the end Kaal has crushed.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲੋਕ ਪਾਲ: guardians of the worlds (the regents of the directions)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[79],"number_text":"੭੯।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਲ ਪਾਣਿ ਜੇ ਜਪੈ। ਅਨੰਤ ਥਾਟ ਤੇ ਥਾਪੈ।","roman":"Kripaal paani je japai | anant thaat te thaapai |","meaning_en":"Those who remember the merciful One (with the sword) in hand, He establishes them in countless ways;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਲ ਪਾਣਿ: read as 'the One with the sword (ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ) in hand' or 'the merciful Lord'. ਅਨੰਤ ਥਾਟ: in endless ways / settings."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇਕਿ ਕਾਲ ਧਿਆਇ ਹੈ। ਜਗਤਿ ਜੀਤ ਜਾਇ ਹੈ। ੭੯।","roman":"Jiteki kaal dhiaai hai | jagti jeet jaai hai | 79 |","meaning_en":"all who meditate on Kaal will go having conquered the world.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[80],"number_text":"੮੦।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਾਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰਯੰ। ਪਰਮਯੰ ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰਯੰ।","roman":"Bachitr chaar chitrayan | paramyan pavitrayan |","meaning_en":"Wondrous and beautiful in form, supreme and pure;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਲੋਕ ਰੂਪ ਰਾਜਿਯੰ। ਸੁਣੇ ਸੁ ਪਾਪ ਭਾਜਿਯੰ। ੮੦।","roman":"Alok roop raajiyan | sune su paap bhaajiyan | 80 |","meaning_en":"His form of unseen splendour shines; hearing (of Him), sin runs away.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[81],"number_text":"੮੧।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਸਾਲ ਲਾਲ ਲੋਚਨੰ। ਬਿਅੰਤ ਪਾਪ ਮੋਚਨੰ।","roman":"Bisaal laal lochnan | biant paap mochnan |","meaning_en":"Large red eyes, the remover of countless sins;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਮਕ ਚੰਦ੍ਰ ਚਾਰਯੰ। ਅਘੀ ਅਨੇਕ ਤਾਰਯੰ। ੮੧।","roman":"Chamak chandr chaaryan | aghee anek taaryan | 81 |","meaning_en":"beautiful, gleaming like the moon, He has carried across many sinners.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਘੀ: sinners."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[82],"number_text":"੮੨।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਲੋਕ ਪਾਲੰ। ਤਿਤੇ ਜੇਰ ਕਾਲੰ।","roman":"Jite lok paalan | tite jer kaalan |","meaning_en":"All the guardians of the worlds are under Kaal;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਸੂਰ ਚੰਦ੍ਰੰ। ਕਹਾ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਬਿੰਦ੍ਰੰ। ੮੨।","roman":"Jite soor chandran | kahaa indr bindran | 82 |","meaning_en":"all the suns and moons; what then of hosts of Indras?","page":142,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਬਿੰਦ੍ਰੰ: Indra and the hosts (of gods)."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[83],"number_text":"੮੩।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰੈ ਚੌਦਹੂੰ ਲੋਕਯੰ ਕਾਲ ਚਕ੍ਰੰ। ਸਭੈ ਨਾਥ ਨਾਥੇ ਭ੍ਰਮੰ ਭਉਹ ਬਕੰ।","roman":"Phirai chaudhoon lokyan kaal chakran | sabhai naath naathe bhraman bhauh bakan |","meaning_en":"The wheel of Kaal turns through the fourteen worlds; all the masters are mastered, wandering under His frowning brow.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਾਥ ਨਾਥੇ: 'the masters are reined in (like animals with a nose-string)'. ਭਉਹ ਬਕ: bent (frowning) brow."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਾ ਰਾਮ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨੰ ਕਹਾ ਚੰਦ ਸੂਰੰ। ਸਭੈ ਹਾਥ ਬਾਧੇ ਖਰੇ ਕਾਲ ਹਜੂਰੰ। ੮੩।","roman":"Kahaa raam krisnan kahaa chand sooran | sabhai haath baadhe khare kaal hajooran | 83 |","meaning_en":"What are Rama and Krishna, what are the moon and sun? All stand with folded hands before Kaal.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸ੍ਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Svaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[84],"number_text":"੮੪।","page":142,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਪਾਇ ਭਯੋ ਭਗਵਾਨ ਸੁ ਜਾਗਤ ਯਾ ਜਗ ਜਾਕੀ ਕਲਾ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaal hee paai bhayo bhagvaan su jaagat yaa jag jaakee kalaa hai |","meaning_en":"By Kaal came Bhagvan (Vishnu), whose power is awake in this world;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਪਾਇ: 'through Kaal' / 'by the will of Kaal'. ਭਗਵਾਨ here is read as Vishnu."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਪਾਇ ਭਯੋ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ ਸਿਵ ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਪਾਇ ਭਯੋ ਜੁਗੀਆ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaal hee paai bhayo brahmaa siv kaal hee paai bhayo jugeeaa hai |","meaning_en":"by Kaal came Brahma and Shiva; by Kaal came the yogi;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਪਾਇ ਸੁਰਾਸੁਰ ਗੰਧ੍ਰਬ ਜਛ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਦਿਸਾ ਬਿਦਿਸਾ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaal hee paai suraasur gandhrab jachh bhujang disaa bidisaa hai |","meaning_en":"by Kaal came gods, demons, gandharvas, yakshas, serpents, and the directions and intermediate directions;","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਸੁਕਾਲ ਸਭੈ ਬਸਿ ਕਾਲ ਕੇ ਏਕ ਹੀ ਕਾਲ ਅਕਾਲ ਸਦਾ ਹੈ। ੮੪।","roman":"Aur sukaal sabhai basi kaal ke ek hee kaal akaal sadaa hai | 84 |","meaning_en":"and all other times are under Kaal; only the one Kaal, the Timeless, is forever.","page":142,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਕਾਲ: read as 'all (other) times / deaths'. ਏਕ ਹੀ ਕਾਲ ਅਕਾਲ: the one Kaal who is (also) Akaal, the Timeless."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[85],"number_text":"੮੫।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵੰ ਨਮੋ ਖੜਗ ਧਾਰੰ। ਸਦਾ ਏਕ ਰੂਪ ਸਦਾ ਨਿਰਬਿਕਾਰੰ।","roman":"Namo dev devan namo kharag dhaaran | sadaa ek roop sadaa nirbikaaran |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the God of gods, salutation to the Bearer of the sword; ever of one form, ever without defect;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਰਾਜਸੰ ਸਾਤਕੰ ਤਾਮਸੇਅੰ। ਨਮੋ ਨਿਰਬਿਕਾਰੰ ਨਮੋ ਨਿਰਜੁਰੇਅੰ। ੮੫।","roman":"Namo raajsan saatkan taamsean | namo nirbikaaran namo nirjurean | 85 |","meaning_en":"salutation to the One in activity, goodness and darkness; salutation to the One without defect, salutation to the One free of affliction.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[86],"number_text":"੮੬।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਬਾਣ ਪਾਣੰ। ਨਮੋ ਨਿਰਭਯਾਣੰ।","roman":"Namo baan paanan | namo nirabhyaanan |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the One with the arrow in hand; salutation to the Fearless;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵੰ। ਭਵਾਣੰ ਭਵੇਅੰ। ੮੬।","roman":"Namo dev devan | bhavaanan bhavean | 86 |","meaning_en":"salutation to the God of gods, in the present and the future.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[87],"number_text":"੮੭।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਖਗ ਖੰਡੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਕਟਾਰੰ। ਸਦਾ ਏਕ ਰੂਪੰ ਸਦਾ ਨਿਰਬਿਕਾਰੰ।","roman":"Namo khag khandan kripaan kataaran | sadaa ek roopan sadaa nirbikaaran |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the sword, the two-edged sword, the kirpan, the dagger; ever of one form, ever without defect;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਗ, ਖੰਡਾ, ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ, ਕਟਾਰ: kinds of sword and dagger, saluted as emblems of the divine power."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਬਾਣ ਪਾਣੰ ਨਮੋ ਦੰਡ ਧਾਰਿਯੰ। ਜਿਨੈ ਚੌਦਹੂੰ ਲੋਕ ਜੋਤੰ ਬਿਥਾਰਿਯੰ।੮੭।","roman":"Namo baan paanan namo dand dhaariyan | jinai chaudhoon lok jotan bithaariyan | 87 |","meaning_en":"salutation to the One with the arrow in hand, salutation to the Bearer of the rod, who spread His light through the fourteen worlds.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[88],"number_text":"੮੮।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮਸਕਾਰਯੰ ਮੋਰ ਤੀਰੰ ਤੁਫੰਗੰ। ਨਮੋ ਖਗ ਅਦਗੰ ਅਭੈਅੰ ਅਭੰਗੰ।","roman":"Namaskaaryan mor teeran tuphangan | namo khag adgan abhaian abhangan |","meaning_en":"My salutation to the arrow and the musket; salutation to the sword, unburnt, fearless, unbreakable;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤੁਫੰਗ: musket. ਅਦਗੰ: read as 'unburnt / unblemished'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਦਾਯੰ ਗ੍ਰਿਸਟੰ ਨਮੋ ਸੈਹਥੀਅੰ। ਜਿਨੈ ਤੁਲੀਯੰ ਬੀਰ ਬੀਯੋ ਨ ਬੀਅੰ। ੮੮।","roman":"Gadaayan gristan namo saihtheean | jinai tuleeyan beer beeyo na beean | 88 |","meaning_en":"to the heavy mace and the lance, salutation; no other hero equals them.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੈਹਥੀ: a lance / spear."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaaval metre.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[89],"number_text":"੮੯।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਚਕ੍ਰ ਪਾਣੰ। ਅਭੂਤੰ ਭਯਾਣੰ।","roman":"Namo chakr paanan | abhootan bhayaanan |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the One with the discus in hand, wondrous and fearsome;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਉਗ੍ਰਦਾੜੰ। ਮਹਾ ਗ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਗਾੜੰ। ੮੯।","roman":"Namo ugradaaran | mahaa grisat gaaran | 89 |","meaning_en":"salutation to the One of fierce tusks, very heavy and firm.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਗਾੜੰ: heavy and strong; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[90],"number_text":"੯੦।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਤੀਰ ਤੋਪੰ। ਜਿਨੈ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਘੋਪੰ।","roman":"Namo teer topan | jinai satr ghopan |","meaning_en":"Salutation to the arrow and the cannon, which have pierced the enemies;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘੋਪੰ: thrust through."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਮੋ ਧੋਪ ਪਟੰ। ਜਿਨੇ ਦੁਸਟ ਦਟੰ। ੯੦।","roman":"Namo dhop patan | jine dusat datan | 90 |","meaning_en":"salutation to the dhop and the patta (swords), which have pressed down the wicked.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧੋਪ, ਪਟਾ: kinds of straight swords."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[91],"number_text":"੯੧।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਮੰ। ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਤਾਮੰ।","roman":"Jite sasatr naaman | namaskaar taaman |","meaning_en":"All the weapons held in the hand by name: salutation to them;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ: weapons held in the hand."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਤੇ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਭੈਯੰ। ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਤੇਯੰ। ੯੧।","roman":"Jite asatr bhaiyan | namaskaar teyan | 91 |","meaning_en":"all the fearsome missiles: salutation to them.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਸਤ੍ਰ: weapons thrown or shot."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸ੍ਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Svaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[92],"number_text":"੯੨।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੇਰੁ ਕਰੋ ਤ੍ਰਿਣ ਤੇ ਮੁਹਿ ਜਾਹਿ ਗਰੀਬ ਨਿਵਾਜ ਨ ਦੂਸਰ ਤੋ ਸੋ।","roman":"Meru karo trin te muhi jaahi gareeb nivaaj na doosar to so |","meaning_en":"He who can make Meru (the great mountain) out of a blade of grass, for me: O Cherisher of the poor, there is none like You.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੇਰੁ ਕਰੋ ਤ੍ਰਿਣ ਤੇ: who turns a straw into Mount Meru, i.e. raises the lowly."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਲ ਛਿਮੋ ਹਮਰੀ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਆਪਨ ਭੂਲਨਹਾਰ ਕਹੂੰ ਕੋਊ ਮੋ ਸੋ।","roman":"Bhool chhimo hamree prabh aapan bhoolanhaar kahoon ko'oo mo so |","meaning_en":"Forgive my mistakes, O Lord, Yourself; where is there anyone who errs like me?","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਵ ਕਰੀ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਤਿਨ ਕੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਦੇਖੀਅਤ ਦ੍ਰਬ ਭਰੋ ਸੋ।","roman":"Sev karee tumree tin ke sabh hee grih dekheeat drab bharo so |","meaning_en":"Those who have served You, their homes are all seen filled with wealth.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾ ਕਲ ਮੈ ਸਭ ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕੇ ਭਾਰੀ ਭੁਜਾਨ ਕੋ ਭਾਰੀ ਭਰੋਸੋ। ੯੨।","roman":"Yaa kal mai sabh kaal kripaan ke bhaaree bhujaan ko bhaaree bharoso | 92 |","meaning_en":"In this age, at all times, my great trust is in the mighty arms of the Sword.","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ: read as 'the Sword of Kaal' or 'Kaal and the Sword'. ਯਾ ਕਲ ਮੈ: in this (Kali) age."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[93],"number_text":"੯੩।","page":143,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਭ ਨਿਸੁੰਭ ਸੇ ਕੋਟ ਨਿਸਚਾਰ ਜਾਹਿ ਛਿਨੇਕ ਬਿਖੈ ਹਨਿ ਡਾਰੇ।","roman":"Sunbh nisunbh se kot nischaar jaahi chhinek bikhai hani daare |","meaning_en":"He who in an instant slew millions of demons like Sumbh and Nisumbh;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸਚਾਰ: night-wanderers (demons)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਧੂਮਰ ਲੋਚਨ ਚੰਡ ਅਉ ਮੁੰਡ ਸੇ ਮਾਹਿਖ ਸੇ ਪਲ ਬੀਚ ਨਿਵਾਰੇ।","roman":"Dhoomar lochan chand au mund se maahikh se pal beech nivaare |","meaning_en":"who in a moment removed the likes of Dhumar Lochan, Chand, Mund and Mahikhasur;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Names of demons slain by the goddess (Durga) in the Puranic stories retold in this granth."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਮਰ ਸੇ ਰਣਿ ਚਿਛਰ ਸੇ ਰਕਤਿਛਣ ਸੇ ਝਟ ਦੈ ਝਝਕਾਰੇ।","roman":"Chaamar se rani chichhar se raktichhan se jhat dai jhajhkaare |","meaning_en":"who swiftly struck down in battle the likes of Chamar, Chichhar and Raktichhan;","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੋ ਸੁ ਸਾਹਿਬੁ ਪਾਇ ਕਹਾ ਪਰਵਾਹ ਰਹੀ ਇਹ ਦਾਸ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ। ੯੩।","roman":"Aiso su saahibu paai kahaa parvaah rahee ih daas tihaare | 93 |","meaning_en":"having found such a Master, what worry remains for this servant of Yours?","page":143,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[94],"number_text":"੯੪।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁੰਡਹੁ ਸੇ ਮਧੁ ਕੀਟਭ ਸੇ ਮੁਰ ਸੇ ਅਘ ਸੇ ਜਿਨਿ ਕੋਟਿ ਦਲੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Mundhu se madhu keetabh se mur se agh se jini koti dale hai |","meaning_en":"Those who had destroyed millions, like Mund, Madhu and Kaitabh, Mur and Agh;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਓਟਿ ਕਰੀ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਨ ਜਿਨੈ ਰਣਿ ਚੋਟ ਪਰੀ ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਟਲੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Oti karee kabhoon na jinai rani chot paree pag dvai na tale hai |","meaning_en":"who never took shelter, and when struck in battle did not move back two steps;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿੰਧੁ ਬਿਖੈ ਜੇ ਨ ਬੂਡੇ ਨਿਸਚਾਰ ਪਾਵਕ ਬਾਣ ਬਹੇ ਨ ਜਲੇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sindhu bikhai je na boode nischaar paavak baan bahe na jale hai |","meaning_en":"demons who did not drown in the ocean, who were not burnt by fiery arrows;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇ ਅਸਿ ਤੋਰਿ ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਅਲੋਕ ਸੁ ਲਾਜ ਕੋ ਛਾਡ ਕੈ ਭਾਜਿ ਚਲੇ ਹੈ। ੯੪।","roman":"Te asi tori biloki alok su laaj ko chhaad kai bhaaji chale hai | 94 |","meaning_en":"seeing Your sword, they abandoned their honour and ran away.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਲੋਕ: read as 'seeing' (together with ਬਿਲੋਕਿ) or 'unseen'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[95],"number_text":"੯੫।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਵਣ ਸੇ ਮਹਿਰਾਵਣ ਸੇ ਘਟਕਾਨਹੁ ਸੇ ਪਲ ਬੀਚ ਪਛਾਰੇ।","roman":"Raavan se mahiraavan se ghatkaanhu se pal beech pachhaare |","meaning_en":"The likes of Ravan, Mahiravan and Ghatkaan (Kumbhkaran), were thrown down in a moment;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਰਦ ਨਾਦ ਅਕੰਪਨ ਸੇ ਜਗ ਜੰਗ ਜੁਰੈ ਜਿਨ ਸਿਉ ਜਮ ਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baarad naad akanpan se jag jang jurai jin siu jam haare |","meaning_en":"those like Baarad Naad (Meghnaad) and Akampan, with whom even Yama lost when they fought;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਰਦ ਨਾਦ: read as Meghnaad ('cloud-roar'), Ravan's son."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਭ ਅਕੁੰਭ ਸੇ ਜੀਤ ਸਭੈ ਜਗਿ ਸਾਤਹੂੰ ਸਿੰਧ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਪਖਾਰੇ।","roman":"Kunbh akunbh se jeet sabhai jagi saathoon sindh hathiaar pakhaare |","meaning_en":"the likes of Kumbh and Akumbh, who conquered the whole world and washed their weapons in all seven seas;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਜੇ ਹੁਤੇ ਅਕਟੇ ਬਿਕਟੇ ਸੁ ਕਟੇ ਕਰਿ ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕੇ ਮਾਰੇ। ੯੫।","roman":"Je je hute akte bikte su kate kari kaal kripaan ke maare | 95 |","meaning_en":"all those who were invincible and fierce were cut down, slain by the sword of Kaal.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[96],"number_text":"੯੬।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਕਹੂੰ ਕਾਲ ਤੇ ਭਾਜ ਕੇ ਬਾਚੀਅਤ ਤੋ ਕਿਹ ਕੁੰਟ ਕਹੋ ਭਜਿ ਜਾਈਯੈ।","roman":"Jo kahoon kaal te bhaaj ke baacheeat to kih kunt kaho bhaji jaaeeyai |","meaning_en":"If one could be saved by running from Kaal, then tell me, in which direction should one run?","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਗੇ ਹੂੰ ਕਾਲ ਧਰੇ ਅਸਿ ਗਾਜਤ ਛਾਜਤ ਹੈ ਜਿਹ ਤੇ ਨਸਿ ਅਈਯੈ।","roman":"Aage hoon kaal dhare asi gaajat chhaajat hai jih te nasi aeeyai |","meaning_en":"Ahead, too, Kaal stands roaring with the sword raised, (so) where can one flee from Him?","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਨ ਕੈ ਗਯੋ ਕੋਈ ਸੁ ਦਾਵ ਰੇ ਜਾਹਿ ਉਪਾਵ ਸੋ ਘਾਵ ਬਚਈਐ।","roman":"Aise na kai gayo koee su daav re jaahi upaav so ghaav bachaeeai |","meaning_en":"No one has ever found such a trick, by whose means the blow can be avoided.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਤੇ ਨ ਛੁਟੀਐ ਮੁੜ ਕਹੂੰ ਹਸਿ ਤਾਕੀ ਨ ਕਿਉ ਸਰਣਾਗਤਿ ਜਈਯੈ। ੯੬।","roman":"Jaate na chhuteeai mur kahoon hasi taakee na kiu sarnaagti jaeeyai | 96 |","meaning_en":"O fool, since there is no escape from Him anywhere, why not gladly go to His refuge?","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁੜ: the edition prints ਮੁੜ, read as ਮੂੜ (fool)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[97],"number_text":"੯੭।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਅਉ ਬਿਸਨੁ ਜਪੇ ਤੁਹਿ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਰਾਮ ਰਹੀਮ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਧਿਆਯੋ।","roman":"Krisan au bisnu jape tuhi kotik raam raheem bhalee bidhi dhiaayo |","meaning_en":"Millions recite Krishna and Vishnu, and worship Ram and Rahim in fine manner;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The line is addressed to the reader ('they recited for you'); ਤੁਹਿ is read as 'you (the worshipper)'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਜਪਿਓ ਅਰੁ ਸੰਭੁ ਥਪਿਓ ਤਹਿ ਤੇ ਤੁਹਿਕੋ ਕਿਨ ਹੂੰ ਨ ਬਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Braham japio aru sanbhu thapio tahi te tuhiko kin hoon na bachaayo |","meaning_en":"Brahma was worshipped and Shambhu (Shiva) installed; yet none of them could save you.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਭੁ ਥਪਿਓ: Shiva was installed (as a lingam)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਟਿ ਕਰੀ ਤਪਸਾ ਦਿਨ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਕਾਹੂ ਨ ਕੌਡੀ ਕੋ ਕਾਮ ਕਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Koti karee tapsaa din kotik kaahoo na kaudee ko kaam kadhaayo |","meaning_en":"Millions did austerities for millions of days; none of it was of a cowrie's worth.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੌਡੀ: a small shell, the least coin."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮ ਕਾ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕਸੀਰੇ ਕੇ ਕਾਮ ਨ ਕਾਲ ਕੋ ਘਾਉ ਕਿਨਹੂੰ ਨ ਬਚਾਯੋ। ੯੭।","roman":"Kaam kaa mantr kaseere ke kaam na kaal ko ghaau kinhoon na bachaayo | 97 |","meaning_en":"The mantras of desire were of no use, not worth a copper; none could save anyone from the blow of Kaal.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਸੀਰਾ: a small copper coin. ਕਾਮ ਕਾ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ: read as 'mantras for one's desires'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[98],"number_text":"੯੮।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹੇ ਕੋ ਕੂਰ ਕਰੇ ਤਪਸਾ ਇਨ ਕੀ ਕੋਊ ਕੌਡੀ ਕੇ ਕਾਮ ਨ ਐਹੈ।","roman":"Kaahe ko koor kare tapsaa in kee ko'oo kaudee ke kaam na aihai |","meaning_en":"Why do you practise false austerities? Not one of them will be of a cowrie's use.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋਹਿ ਬਚਾਇ ਸਕੈ ਕਹੁ ਕੈਸੇ ਕੈ ਆਪਨ ਘਾਵ ਬਚਾਇ ਨ ਐਹੈ।","roman":"Tohi bachaai sakai kahu kaise kai aapan ghaav bachaai na aihai |","meaning_en":"Tell me, how can they save you, when they cannot save themselves from the blow?","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਕਰਾਲ ਕੀ ਪਾਵਕ ਕੁੰਡ ਮੈ ਆਪਿ ਟੰਗਿਓ ਤਿਮ ਤੋਹਿ ਟੰਗੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kop karaal kee paavak kund mai aapi tangio tim tohi tangai hai |","meaning_en":"Into the fire-pit of fearsome wrath they themselves are hung, and so will they hang you.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਾਵਕ ਕੁੰਡ: fire-pit. ਟੰਗਿਓ: hung, suspended."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੇਤ ਰੇ ਚੇਤ ਅਜੋ ਜੀਅ ਮੈ ਜੜ ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾ ਬਿਨੁ ਕਾਮ ਨ ਐਹੈ। ੯੮।","roman":"Chet re chet ajo jeea mai jar kaal kripaa binu kaam na aihai | 98 |","meaning_en":"Wake up, wake up even now in your heart, O fool: without the grace of Kaal nothing will help.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[99],"number_text":"੯੯।","page":144,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹਿ ਪਛਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਨ ਮਹਾ ਪਸੁ ਜਾ ਕੋ ਪ੍ਰਤਾਪੁ ਤਿਹੂੰ ਪੁਰ ਮਾਹੀ।","roman":"Taahi pachhaanat hai na mahaa pasu jaa ko prataapu tihoon pur maahee |","meaning_en":"The great beast (fool) does not recognise Him whose glory fills the three worlds;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਜਤ ਹੈ ਪਰਮੇਸਰ ਕੈ ਜਿਹ ਕੈ ਪਰਸੈ ਪਰਲੋਕ ਪਰਾਹੀ।","roman":"Poojat hai parmesar kai jih kai parsai parlok paraahee |","meaning_en":"he worships as the Supreme Lord those whose touch drives away the next world (salvation);","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The line is read in several ways; the sense is that one worships things that lead away from liberation."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕਰੋ ਪਰਮਾਰਥ ਕੈ ਜਿਹ ਪਾਪਨ ਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਪਾਪ ਲਜਾਈ।","roman":"Paap karo parmaarath kai jih paapan te ati paap lajaaee |","meaning_en":"he commits sins in the name of holiness, sins at which even the worst sin is ashamed;","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਰਮਾਰਥ: spiritual good, holiness."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇ ਪਰੋ ਪਰਮੇਸਰ ਕੇ ਜੜ ਪਾਹਨ ਮੈ ਪਰਮੇਸਰ ਨਾਹੀ। ੯੯।","roman":"Paai paro parmesar ke jar paahan mai parmesar naahee | 99 |","meaning_en":"O fool, fall at the feet of the Supreme Lord: the Supreme Lord is not in a stone.","page":144,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[100],"number_text":"੧੦੦।","page":145,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਨ ਭਜੇ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨ ਤਜੇ ਨਹੀ ਭੇਖ ਸਜੇ ਨਹੀ ਮੂੰਡ ਮੁੰਡਾਏ।","roman":"Mon bhaje nahee maan taje nahee bhekh saje nahee moond mundaae |","meaning_en":"Not by keeping silence, not by giving up pride, not by adorning a sectarian garb, not by shaving the head;","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੰਠਿ ਨ ਕੰਠੀ ਕਠੋਰ ਧਰੈ ਨਹੀ ਸੀਸ ਜਟਾਨ ਕੇ ਜੂਟ ਸੁਹਾਏ।","roman":"Kanthi na kanthee kathor dharai nahee sees jataan ke joot suhaae |","meaning_en":"not by wearing a hard necklace round the neck, nor by adorning the head with knots of matted hair;","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਚੁ ਕਹੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਲੈ ਚਿਤੁ ਦੈ ਬਿਨੁ ਦੀਨ ਦਿਆਲ ਕੀ ਸਾਮ ਸਿਧਾਏ।","roman":"Saachu kaho suni lai chitu dai binu deen diaal kee saam sidhaae |","meaning_en":"I tell the truth, listen with attention: without the protection of the Merciful to the humble, (all) depart (in vain).","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਾਮ: refuge, protection. ਸਿਧਾਏ: depart (from this world)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਕਰੇ ਪ੍ਰਭੁ ਪਾਯਤ ਹੈ ਕਿਰਪਾਲ ਨ ਭੀਜਤ ਲਾਂਡ ਕਟਾਏ। ੧੦੦।","roman":"Preeti kare prabhu paayat hai kirpaal na bheejat laand kataae | 100 |","meaning_en":"By love the Lord is found; the Merciful is not pleased by cutting off the genitals.","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲਾਂਡ ਕਟਾਏ: self-castration, an extreme ascetic practice, given as an example of useless austerity."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[101],"number_text":"੧੦੧।","page":145,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗਦ ਦੀਪ ਸਭੈ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਅਰ ਸਾਤ ਸਮੁੰਦ੍ਰਨ ਕੀ ਮਸੁ ਕੈਹੋ।","roman":"Kaagad deep sabhai kari kai ar saat samundran kee masu kaiho |","meaning_en":"If I made all the continents into paper, and the seven seas into ink;","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਸੁ: ink."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਟਿ ਬਨਾਸਪਤੀ ਸਿਗਰੀ ਲਿਖਬੇ ਹੂੰ ਕੇ ਲੇਖਨ ਕਾਜਿ ਬਨੈਹੋ।","roman":"Kaati banaasaptee sigree likhbe hoon ke lekhan kaaji banaiho |","meaning_en":"if I cut down all the vegetation and made it into pens for writing;","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਰਸੁਤੀ ਬਕਤਾ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਜੁਗ ਕੋਟਿ ਗਨੇਸ ਕੈ ਹਾਥਿ ਲਿਖੈਹੋ।","roman":"Saarsutee baktaa kari kai jug koti ganes kai haathi likhaiho |","meaning_en":"if I made Saraswati the speaker, and had Ganesh write with his hand for millions of ages;","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Saraswati: goddess of learning and speech; Ganesh is traditionally the scribe."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਬਿਨਾ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਨ ਤਊ ਤੁਮ ਕੋ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਨੈਕੁ ਰਿਝੈਹੋ। ੧੦੧।","roman":"Kaal kripaan binaa bintee na taoo tum ko prabh naiku rijhaiho | 101 |","meaning_en":"even then, O Lord of the Sword of Kaal, without supplication I could not please You in the least.","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ: read as an address, 'O Kaal, wielder of the sword'. ਬਿਨਾ ਬਿਨਤੀ: read as 'without humble prayer' or 'apart from prayer'."}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਾਲ ਜੀ ਕੀ ਉਸਤਤਿ","roman":"Iti sree bachitr naatak granthe sree kaal jee kee usatti","meaning_en":"Thus ends, in the book Bachittar Natak, the praise of the revered Kaal,","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਿਥਮ ਧਿਆਇ ਸੰਪੂਰਨੰ ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ। ੧।","roman":"Pritham dhiaai sanpoornan satu subham satu | 1 |","meaning_en":"the first chapter, complete. All is true and auspicious. 1.","page":145,"meaning_status":"draft"}],"page":145,"number":[1]}});
